{title: Precious Memories}
{artist: J. B. F. Wright}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 3/4}
# Published 1925.

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Precious mem'ries, [C]unseen [G]angels
Sent from [D7]somewhere to my [G]soul
How they [G]linger, [C]ever [G]near me
And the [D7]sacred past un[G]fold
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Precious mem'ries, [C]how they [G]linger
How they [D7]ever flood my [G]soul
In the [G]stillness [C]of the [G]midnight
[D7]Precious, sacred scenes un[G]fold
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Precious father, [C]loving [G]mother
Fly a[D7]cross the lonely [G]years
And old [G]home scenes [C]of my [G]childhood
In fond [D7]memory ap[G]pear
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
As I [G]travel [C]on life's [G]pathway
Know not [D7]what the years may [G]hold
As I [G]ponder, [C]hope grows [G]fonder
[D7]Precious mem'ries flood my [G]soul
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
